	public static readonly (string Id, string Description, string EvidenceNeeded)[] All =
	{
		("PTCL-900", "The key's pose is read from the current animator hierarchy when the EVENT runs; the original reads the key-table matrices refreshed by the object's last draw (tp.exe 0x473C70 -> 0x44AB30, gated by instance-header bit 0x1 and table bit 0x1), so the frozen start position differs from the original's by the animation advanced since the last render and is not stale while the object is culled", "A per-object last-drawn-pose cache, and a capture to confirm the frame lag (the draw-callback dispatch 0x463030 is a function pointer and was not traced further)"),
		("PTCL-904", "A particle's quad half-height is size / 1024 original units as in tp.exe 0x57C620; the width multiplies it by the frame record's float +8 (textured) or the projection aspect DAT_008BCBCC (untextured) in the original, while OpenTPW uses the sprite frame's pixel aspect and 1; the sprite UVs cover the whole frame", "Where the sprite loader writes the 24-byte frame record's float +8, and what DAT_008BCBCC holds"),
		("PTCL-905", "OpenTPW groups the quads into three blend batches (alpha, source-alpha-over-one, one-plus-one), each in emitter slot order, depth-tested without depth writes and not depth sorted; the original submits one primitive per particle, slots 0..119 ascending and newest particle first, each with its own state word (untextured 0x1256 or 0x556, flags bit 4 0x200522 plus 0x30 for bit 0x2000, 0x20000 and world 0x800), and whether its engine queue depth-sorts (tp.exe 0x565F90) is untraced; an untextured particle with neither flag draws as alpha", "The engine queue's sorting at 0x565F90 and 0x565240, and the untextured alpha-test state words"),
		("PTCL-906", "The engine position of an EVENT is converted back to native units (world floats * 1024, truncated as the original's _ftol does) by inverting OpenTPW's placement (0.2 engine units per original unit, the park heightfield's centring, Z-up to Y-up); the pool runs with the options' built-in default PARTICLEDENSITY (500) and 2048 particles, the user's saved density value is not read and the option is not exposed, and the terrain-height callback is the original's flat-zero stub", "The registry value of PARTICLEDENSITY on a real install, and a side-by-side of an original EVENT position against the converted one"),
		("PTCL-908", "Only EVENT 1/2 and ADDOBJ 1/2 (tp.exe 0x551F5F, 0x5522C5) start particle effects: ADDOBJ keeps the handle for KILLOBJ but the effect does not follow the key node on later scheduler runs (0x5516B0 calls 0x51FE30 with the node position truncated to whole units), ADDOBJ_EXT (opcode 9, which carries the control operand) has no VM handler, the saved object records do not hold the handles, a negative key (the object's box centre, 0x556B90/0x466B70), a scoped effect (bit 0x8000, the per-type slot table at record +0x4E0, 0x4145D0) and an unresolved key start nothing, and the ~25 other engine callers of 0x521E60/0x521930 are not wired", "The key-node follow of ADDOBJ records (0x551943 and 0x551B30 for type 2), the VM handler of opcode 9, where record +0x4E0 is filled, and the callers' triggers and operands"),
